{"availability":"available","full":"ShaneOnChain/rarityscope","name":"rarityscope","description":"Fork-first NFT rarity browser — three switchable rarity methods, one config file. Ships with a generated demo collection.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-08T16:49:03Z","updated":"2026-07-09T03:48:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rarityscope.vercel.app","topics":["nextjs","nft","open-source","openrarity","rarity","xrpl"],"demo":"https://rarityscope.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.605Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.605Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.605Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.605Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hostable, mobile-first rarity browser for any NFT collection. Search a piece, see its rank and full trait breakdown, browse the whole collection, and compare two side by side. Rank the same collection three different ways and flip between them with one tap.","RarityScope is fork-first: everything specific to a collection lives in one config file and one CSS file, so pointing it at your own collection is a few edits and a data build — no code changes.","Ships with scopelings, a 100-piece generated demo collection whose art and metadata live in the repo (scripts/demo/ regenerates them) — so the template works out of the box without bundling any real project's art. Built by XRPLClaw. MIT licensed. Not financial advice."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ShaneOnChain/rarityscope/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c13fa4339653118cc7304518e230622d3831ed4519fc25d1fa0ed57a1d32fbd7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.775Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:35.775Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-hostable, mobile-first rarity browser for any NFT collection. Search a piece, see its rank and